cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BitGraph in your research, please cite it using the metadata in this file, and cite the papers behind the algorithms you use (see the README)."
type: software
title: "BitGraph: bit-parallel sets and graphs for combinatorial optimization"
abstract: "BitGraph is a C++ library for fast set and graph operations. BITSCAN provides dense and sparse bitsets with very fast bit scanning, GRAPH represents graphs as bitsets, and UTILS provides supporting utilities."
authors:
  - family-names: "San Segundo"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    affiliation: "Centro de Automática y Robótica (CAR), UPM-CSIC"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/psanse/BitGraph"
url: "https://github.com/psanse/BitGraph"
keywords:
  - bitset
  - bit-parallelism
  - graph algorithms
  - combinatorial optimization
  - maximum clique
  - C++
